  "scope": "Universal degree-13 field-norm decomposition, homogeneous polynomial coordinates and nonzero residue exactly for distinct labels; 37-node and 25-node descents, plus Galois-orbit compression the five-term tensor formula and paired determinants, giving 1600000000 base-field determinants for every prime >= 37. The 18-form checkpoint gives 850305600 determinants for primes >= 37 congruent to 1 mod 3, with root existence proved. The degree-7 checkpoint gives 75816 determinants over the same primes, with homogeneous coordinates and the distinct-label criterion. The degree-5 checkpoint gives 2916 determinants, with the same interfaces; the two-repeated-column determinant factorization is also checked. The finite tagged digit model, exact joint tails, carry implication, tag valuation, minor-exponent moment, column reindexing and label-mixture bound are kernel-checked.",
